judge_raw_output:
The population has likely been driven into a narrow, low-spread but low-quality region by the heavy spread penalty (weight 0.6). Lowering that weight should restore exploration and let the optimizer prioritize quality_score. Evidence: quality_score mean 0.026459 (best 0.123464) while parameter_spread mean improved from ~0.2275 → 0.10458 under the current weight 0.6; parameter_mean also dropped 0.7176 → 0.631929, consistent with an unintended shift. I'll therefore reduce the penalty on spread so the optimizer can seek higher-quality, higher-spread candidates.

